cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this firmware, please cite it as below."
title: "shinto: Arduino firmware for peak-end-rule electroshock experiments in Drosophila"
abstract: >-
  shinto is an Arduino-Uno firmware that drives a 128-step programmable
  electric-shock source for Drosophila aversive conditioning. It supports
  classic Tully-style two-session stimulus trains and a pattern-stimulus
  engine that emits voltage templates with optional terminal spikes, used
  to test the peak-end rule in retrospective evaluation of aversive
  episodes.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Bart R. H."
    family-names: "Geurten"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1816-3241"
    affiliation: "Department of Zoology, University of Otago, Dunedin, New Zealand"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zerotonin/shinto"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - Drosophila
  - aversive conditioning
  - peak-end rule
  - Tully trigger
  - Arduino
  - electrophysiology
  - cuewire
  - PARROTard
